        'events, and most of the remaining events were inconclusive (Figures 2A, B, Table S8). Thus, a comparison of a single human and '
        'a single mouse dataset (Figure 2C) cannot separate species differences from dataset differences, and we '
        'classified each event in each cell type from the PSI of all five '
        'datasets (Figure 1C), without using a P value: an event was classified as differentially spliced between species if, for at least '
        'one of its junctions, the PSI of every human dataset differed from the PSI of every mouse dataset by at '
        'least 0.1 (high confidence, at least 0.2), that is, if the human-mouse difference was larger than any '
